# URL rules for the CSM Synergy site.
#
# These mirror the site's OBSERVED live behaviour, which is not the same as a
# literal reading of netlify.toml. Netlify serves a matching static file before
# it applies redirect rules, so several rules in that file never fired — most
# notably `/leadership-call -> /construction-founders-mastermind 301`, which
# lost to leadership-call.html and returns 200 in production. Porting the config
# verbatim would have introduced redirects that do not exist today.
#
# Only paths with NO file of their own need a rule here. Everything else
# (/about, /contact, /integrations, ...) is resolved by html_handling
# "auto-trailing-slash", which serves about.html for /about.
#
# Rewrite targets are deliberately EXTENSIONLESS. Pointing a 200 at
# "/foo.html" makes html_handling normalise the .html away with a 307 back to
# "/foo", which then re-enters this rule and loops.

# No home.html exists, so this rule fires. It needed Netlify's "!" force flag
# there; here a plain 301 is correct.
/home                                             /                                  301

# Renamed offer. No file by either name, so both rules apply.
/synergy-leadership-circle                        /construction-founders-mastermind  301
/construction-founders-mastermind                 /leadership-call                   200

# Blog posts live as flat blog-<slug>.html files but are linked as /blog/<slug>.
/blog/why-construction-salespeople-lose-deals     /blog-post                         200
/blog/crm-costing-you-deals                       /blog-crm-costing-you-deals        200
/blog/stop-being-the-bottleneck                   /blog-stop-being-the-bottleneck    200
/blog/post-frame-local-seo                        /blog-post-frame-local-seo         200
/blog/shed-sales-follow-up                        /blog-shed-sales-follow-up         200
/blog/smartbuild-ghl-integration                  /blog-smartbuild-ghl-integration   200
